<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions 60 mln rupees of six-month bonds.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions 60 mln rupees of six-month bonds.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it had auctioned six-month federal bonds worth a total of 60 million rupees in an open market operation (OMO) on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said bids worth 680 million rupees were submitted, out of which 60 million rupees were accepted for the outright sale of six-month bonds at a maximum cut-off of 16.50 percent.</p>
<p>In the previous OMO held on December 5 bids worth 750 billion rupees were submitted, all of which were accepted for the outright sale of the bonds at the same cut-off.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
